## 1. Scope

This license covers original Songlass source code, documentation and artwork
that a copyright holder offers under these terms (the "Software"). Each holder
grants permissions only for material they have the right to license. Ownership
remains with the respective copyright holders.

Separately licensed dependencies, fonts, data and other third-party material
remain governed by their own terms. This license does not replace their notices
or restrict rights you receive under those terms or applicable mandatory law.
It does not revoke permissions already granted for earlier copies under another
license.

## 2. Personal use

You may obtain, inspect, study, compile, run and modify the Software for your own
personal, noncommercial use. You may keep personal backups and install your
personal builds on your own devices. Private changes do not have to be submitted
to the project.

These permissions do not authorize sharing copies with others except as allowed
by section 3 or by written permission under section 4.

## 3. Contributions and review

You may create and share working source forks, patches and pull requests solely
to prepare, discuss, evaluate or contribute changes to Songlass. You may compile
and run the Software in development and continuous-integration environments and
share development or review builds for that contribution workflow.

Public working forks are permitted. Clearly identify a fork or build as
unofficial development or review material, retain this license and applicable
copyright notices, and make its source available to its reviewers. Do not
present it as an official release or market it as a separate player. Receiving
payment for development or review work does not remove these permissions.

You may use the Songlass name, project identifiers and original artwork as
needed to identify and test that contribution, including changes needed to
install a development build alongside the official app. This is not permission
to imply endorsement or use the branding for a separate product.

By intentionally submitting original material for inclusion in Songlass, you
offer the material you have the right to license under this license, unless the
maintainers accept separate written terms. You retain copyright. Submission
does not assign ownership or grant an unrestricted right to relicense your work.
Identify third-party material and its separate terms when submitting it.

## 4. Distribution and commercial restrictions

Except for the contribution and review activities allowed by section 3, you
need prior written permission from the relevant copyright holders to:

- Distribute, publish, sublicense or sell the Software, in source or binary
  form, whether unchanged or modified.
- Offer an app, service or other product incorporating the Software, including
  a free or paid clone, a renamed player or a repackaged build.
- Rebrand or advertise a distributed version as a different product.
- Use the Software commercially beyond the paid contribution work allowed by
  section 3.

A store or repository may redistribute unchanged official builds free of charge
only when authorized in writing by the project owner. It must retain the
official branding, this license and all applicable notices. That authorization
does not permit modified builds or imply a right to sublicense the Software.
Separate written permission may specify other authorized uses.

## 5. Notices and branding

Retain copyright, license and third-party attribution notices in copies you are
permitted to make or share. Do not misrepresent authorship, provenance or
official status. No general trademark permission or endorsement is granted;
the limited identification and testing permission in section 3 remains valid.

